UNIT boundedFilter
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY spec
SIG boundedFilter(array, concurrency, gate) -> Promise<Array<number>>
DESCRIPTION Filters an integer array to retain only even numbers in their original input order, subject to a concurrency bound.
DESCRIPTION For each array element, the unit examines whether the element is even. The examination is signaled to the harness by awaiting gate.open(element).
DESCRIPTION The gate parameter is a harness-owned completion source: gate.open(element) is a COMPLETION SOURCE that resolves with the element unchanged and performs no computation, transformation, or filtering.
DESCRIPTION The UNIT performs all domain work: it determines whether each element is even and includes only even elements in the output array. The gate only signals timing to the verifier, never performs any work.
DESCRIPTION No more than concurrency examinations may be in flight (awaiting gate.open()) at any instant.
PAR Each element examination is independent and runs concurrently; the harness interleaves the resolutions of gate.open() calls.
INVARIANT At most min(concurrency, array.length) gate.open() calls may be in flight (awaited but not yet resolved) simultaneously.
INVARIANT An examination is in flight from the instant gate.open(element) is awaited until it resolves.
INVARIANT The result is an array containing exactly those elements e from the input where (e % 2 === 0), meaning e modulo 2 equals 0.
INVARIANT The result preserves the original input order: if input elements at indices i and j satisfy i < j and both are even, they appear in that relative order in the result.
INVARIANT For empty input array, the result is an empty array and no gate.open() calls are made.
INVARIANT Each input element is examined exactly once for evenness, regardless of the order in which gate.open() calls resolve.
